8261	{"artifactId":"LLD-ab934d0926ef5dc7-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-ab934d0926ef5dc7-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-16T10:48:57.207Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every stated decision (cheap default → cli-claude/haiku, Codex install → gpt-6-astra/gpt-6.1-sol/gpt-6-luna, catalog lists those three, existing configs untouched) is designed across DEFAULT_TIERS, config catalog, plugin manifest, both installer copies and the cloud catalog","evidence":"Every site that holds the old value is named in §3: src/config/analyze.ts:126 cheap ollama/qwen3.6:27b; config-catalog.ts:108-109; vscode-plugin/package.json:323,334; scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:292-305 (identical lines in vscode-plugin/assets copy); cloud-model-catalog.json:11-13 gpt-5-codex/gpt-5/o4-mini. No non-goal (e.g. rewriting existing config.json, models.local.coreModel) is built. [files: src/config/analyze.ts, src/config/config-catalog.ts, vscode-plugin/package.json, scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh, src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"resolveTiers fills every unnamed tier from DEFAULT_TIERS and assembleConfig stores the full tiers, so the role router's legacy/clientDefault fallback branch is never reached by assembled configs","evidence":"analyze.ts:225-231 resolveTiers returns `tiering.tiers?.cheap ?? DEFAULT_TIERS.cheap`; :257 `tiering: { ...tiering, tiers }`. role-router.ts:135-136 `configuredTier = byRepo?.tiers?.[tier] ?? cfg.tiering.tiers?.[tier]`, which is always defined, so `(legacyExplicit ? undefined : DEFAULT_TIERS[tier])` never runs. [files: src/config/analyze.ts, src/analyze/context/role-router.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"buildSummariserProvider pins a CLI model only when summariserModelExplicit is true, so on the built-in default it would spawn the CLI with no model","evidence":"shaper-provider.ts:283 `const model = cfg.summariserModelExplicit && cfg.summariserModel !== '' ? cfg.summariserModel : undefined;` and analyze.ts:254 sets summariserModelExplicit only when tiering.tiers?.cheap?.model was set in config. [files: src/analyze/context/shaper-provider.ts, src/config/analyze.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A cheap tier with a runner but an empty or missing model is ignored at parse time with a warning, so the built-in default applies","evidence":"analyze.ts:351-353 `if (!isRunner(runner) || typeof model !== 'string' || model.length === 0) { log.warn(... 'ignored'); continue; }` [files: src/config/analyze.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test files src/config/__tests__/tier-defaults.test.ts and src/daemon/__tests__/model-catalog-asset.test.ts are new, while model-tiers.test.ts with the named title and the plugin's manifest-catalog test are reused","evidence":"Glob finds neither tier-defaults.test.ts nor model-catalog-asset.test.ts, so both must be created; §6 step 4 says 'update or add the tests'. model-tiers.test.ts:27 holds the exact title 'empty tiering: tiers = DEFAULT_TIERS (source default), coreFloor = mid (default)'. vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/manifest-catalog.test.ts exists. [files: src/cli/__tests__/model-tiers.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/manifest-catalog.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/model-catalog.test.ts]","action":"Build should create both new test files. The existing model-catalog.test.ts uses fixtures (gpt-5-codex) and needs no change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The test inventory pinning the old defaults is complete (tests that must be updated)","evidence":"grep 'qwen3.6:27b' over *.test.ts: only model-tiers.test.ts:31 pins cheap = ollama/qwen3.6:27b (tui.test and party.test use it as an unrelated fixture). No vscode-plugin/src test pins qwen3.6:27b or gpt-5. summariser-provider.test.ts tests use a hand-built cfg fixture (summariserModelExplicit:false), so they still pass after the pin change. They are not named as change sites but are not broken. [files: src/cli/__tests__/model-tiers.test.ts, src/analyze/context/__tests__/summariser-provider.test.ts]","action":"Optionally add a summariser-provider.test case for the non-explicit CLI pin next to the planned tier-defaults test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Comments naming the summariser as local are all listed (role-router lines 80/132, analyze.ts 170-178, buildSummariserProvider doc)","evidence":"role-router.ts:132 says 'peripheral→local' and :200 says 'summariser-stays-local decoupling'. The design names lines 80 and 132 but not 200. analyze.ts:170-177 and shaper-provider.ts:265-275/281-282 match what the design says. [files: src/analyze/context/role-router.ts]","action":"Also update the role-router.ts:200 comment ('summariser-stays-local') during the build. LOW.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing config.json files that name their tiers keep them, and model ids are free strings, so configs naming catalog-removed models still resolve","evidence":"analyze.ts:345-356 accepts any non-empty string model with no catalog check. resolveTiers prefers the parsed tier over DEFAULT_TIERS. The installer heredoc only writes tiers when it creates the file (design §3.4). The catalog is consumed only by model-catalog.ts for the picker. [files: src/config/analyze.ts, src/daemon/model-catalog.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A cheap-tier role or summariser on a machine without the claude binary fails as an error, not silently; this is accepted with no pre-check","evidence":"The summariser builds `new CliProvider({ kind: cliKind, ... })` (shaper-provider.ts:285) and cheap roles go through buildShaperProvider's CLI branch (:230-251), both with no local fallback, so a missing binary surfaces through CliProvider's subprocess failure. The design states the handling and user impact for this case, for a rejected model id, and for quota cost. [files: src/analyze/context/shaper-provider.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac1-ac3 each map to concrete tests that can carry them","evidence":"§5 acceptance mapping covers ac1 (model-tiers.test.ts:27 existing title, plus new tier-defaults tests), ac2 (installer and catalog contract tests, plugin-copy identity) and ac3 (role-router configured-cheap-wins, summariser pin). The plugin's manifest-catalog.test.ts compares manifest defaults with the catalog, which pins the package.json change. [files: src/cli/__tests__/model-tiers.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/manifest-catalog.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":10,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-16T10:48:57.207Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
